<section id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details and parameters.</h4>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For tasks using BEVDet and FlashOcc as the occupancy network, we employ a ResNet-50 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. 2016</a>)</cite> backbone, with an image resolution of <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 704" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>704</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 704</annotation></semantics></math> and a 2D feature dimension <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> set to 768 . For TPVFormer, we follow the settings of POP3D<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vobecky et al. 2023</a>)</cite>. Training is conducted using the AdamW optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov 2017</a>)</cite> with a learning rate of <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient clipping, over a total of 24 epochs. We set <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{2}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{2}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>,for a detailed hyperparameter sensitivity analysis, please refer to Appendix. Most experiments are conducted on 6 NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 GPUs.</p>
</div>
